# s6_dealer_window
#
# lever      dealer writes key material to disk and rewinds after every operation (buffer holds one
#            of 97 operations); online phase maps the file and returns consumed pages behind its
#            read position. patches/patch_key_window.py (file, mapping) + patches/patch_dealer_window.py
#            (rewind, 1 GiB buffer).
#
# impl_lever: patches/patch_key_window.py patches/patch_keywindow_probe.py patches/patch_dealer_window.py
# Two levers (key_window, dealer_window); the p_keywindow probe between them is carried by this binary.
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: main
# cost_class: paid
# evidence: exact
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# measured
#   peak_host_kb      19,052,324 -> 2,139,588   -16,912,736 kB   -88.77%
#   factor over s5                                                8.90x in one step
#   factor over s0    34,522,940 -> 2,139,588                    16.13x
#   W_host                 85.72 ->      9.64
#   wall                      27 ->         63 s
#   gate              comm:1062390674 keys:18075947008, byte-identical to s5, s4, s3, s2 and s0
#   marker            SNNI_BUF|keybuf_used=18075947008|keybuf_alloc=1073741824
#                     (16.83 GiB through a 1 GiB buffer, 97 rewinds)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tables
#   s5_keybuf_tight                                      s6_dealer_window
#   18,387.8 MB  0.943  heap:main <- gpu_mem.cu:77:cpuMalloc     -- absent --
#      453.3 MB  0.023  heap:GPUBERT::GPUBERT                    453.3 MB  0.207
#      226.6 MB  0.012  heap:main <- bert.h:89:GPUBERT           226.6 MB  0.103
#      134.2 MB  0.007  heap:SigmaPeer::initCommBufs             134.2 MB  0.061
#                                                                134.2 MB  0.061  heap:SIGMAKeygen::SIGMAKeygen
#   attributed 19,507 MB                                  attributed 1,252 MB
# Declared object (94.3% of s5) absent; the 1 GiB window (134.2 MB resident at the peak) appears
# under its constructor. Next object: GPUBERT::GPUBERT, 453.3 MB (20.7%).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rewind     all eight keyBuf sites append (seven generators: matmul, gelu, silu, layernorm, mha,
#            mul, truncate; one `keyBuf += memSz` after moveIntoCPUMem in output()). startPtr read
#            only in keySize = keyBuf - startPtr and the file write. Nothing reads back.
# window     p_keywindow_high (no allocation change):
#              SNNI_KW|op_high=825125000|ops=97|keysize=18075946656
#            787 MiB vs 16.83 GiB (21.9x), mean 178 MiB; buffer 1 GiB (1.30x). close() assert
#            rewritten to bound the window; build checks it with grep -a (strings absent on compute
#            nodes after module purge).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# history
# 1. s6_key_window (job 46262407) died in 41 s on both parties, gpu_mem.cu:91 code 713
#    cudaErrorHostMemoryNotRegistered: an explicit cpuFree(sigmaKeygen->startPtr, true) duplicated
#    close()'s free. Removed (stock: empty filename, the same buffer is passed on as
#    sigma->keyBuf = sigmaKeygen->startPtr).
# 2. s6_key_window then measured -0.71%, refused: "host objects sampled at 2,060,672 kB, 89.1% below
#    the 18,916,820 kB peak" (object -99.3%; VmHWM set by the dealer fill). Off-path; origin of this step.
# 3. first build of this step refused at an anchor (`keyBufSz = 17 * OneGB` indented eight spaces,
#    eight model branches); anchor now includes the following line. Patches are dry-run against a
#    copy of the real tree before building.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cost       paid: 27 -> 63 s (+133%), 17 GB written and read over a network filesystem.
#            s6_key_window (one blocking write at close()) took 66 s.
# defect     SNNI_KW reports keysize=0 here (probe fprintf in close() precedes the new
#            keySize = kwWritten + tail). Real figure in the gate (KEYS:18075947008). Not fixed
#            (would require rebuild and re-measurement).
